 <article><h2>Format and execution boundary</h2><p>Bounded, finite grayscale TIFF: little/big endian, classic TIFF or small BigTIFF, uncompressed strips. Atlas imports require the exact declared placement profile and matching sample checksum. Unsupported metadata, compression or page stacking is rejected.</p><p>The corpus's language, mechanics and OME-Zarr proposals remain separate. This adapter does not execute metadata or turn TIFF pixels into independent silicon, optical hardware, or a complete RUSSL/MSSL runtime.</p></article></div></section>
 <section id="commands" class="view"><div class="section-heading"><div class="eyebrow">REFERENCE</div><h1>Every command, one place.</h1><p>Search the live registry. “Insert” fills the command line without executing anything.</p></div><input type="search" id="search-commands" placeholder="Search names, descriptions, or usage" aria-label="Search commands"><div id="command-count" class="fine"></div><div id="command-list" class="command-list"></div></section>
 <section id="storage" class="view"><div class="section-heading"><div class="eyebrow">ORIGIN-SCOPED STORAGE</div><h1>Your virtual volume.</h1><p>Two MiB of file contents, up to 1,500 nodes. Browser storage is not a backup and may be cleared or evicted.</p></div><div class="storage-actions"><button id="sync">Sync volume</button><button id="backup">Download backup</button><button id="previous-backup">Previous committed backup</button><button id="restore">Restore backup…</button><button id="persist">Request persistent storage</button><input id="restore-file" type="file" accept="application/json,.json" hidden></div><p id="storage-status" class="fine">No volume status yet.</p><form id="path-form"><label for="path">VFS path</label><input id="path" value="/var/hpu" maxlength="4096"><button>Open directory</button><button id="parent" type="button">Parent</button></form><div id="file-list"></div><p class="fine">Paths here belong to the virtual filesystem, not C:\ or D:\. Only selected exports are downloaded to your computer. Restore replaces the virtual volume after validation and preserves its previous committed revision.</p></section>
-<section id="system" class="view"><div class="section-heading"><div class="eyebrow">EXECUTION BOUNDARY</div><h1>What this build actually does.</h1></div><div class="system-grid"><article><h2>Console → worker → storage</h2><p>A local static Node server opens this browser application. Each terminal uses a dedicated MessageChannel with bounded, sequenced binary frames. No network WebSocket or native terminal process is opened.</p><p>The SPIRAL shell has quoting, variables, aliases, pipelines, redirects, history, and a bounded virtual filesystem. It is not Bash, PowerShell, or a host operating system.</p></article><article><h2>Software, not silicon acceleration</h2><p>The field simulator computes Fourier propagation, optical gate models, phase retrieval, GIF spooling, and LUT transformations in JavaScript. “GPU” loops in the input package are batched CPU loops, not hardware offload.</p><p>Landauer-related values are transition-cost proxies, not measured heat. Bloch, Wigner, and penteract values are model-derived visualizations, not measurements of quantum hardware or physical five-dimensional storage.</p></article><article><h2>Data protection</h2><p>A single-writer Web Lock and transactional revision checks prevent cooperating windows from overwriting one another. Recovery validates snapshots before replacing live state. Corrupt data never triggers a factory reset.</p><p>Checksums detect accidental changes; they are not signatures or authentication. Keep exported backups. Old releases do not honor the new lock protocol and should not run on the same origin.</p></article><article><h2>Release 2.2.1</h2><p>No third-party runtime package installation. Original research attachments remain unchanged under references/. The removed cloud/auth scaffold and original generated outputs are retained in audit/legacy-scaffold.zip, not served by the app.</p><p>See AUDIT_REPORT.md, CHANGELOG.md, and the reproducible test suite in the release folder. Windows launchers provision a hash-verified private Node.js runtime on first use. No system Node.js installation is required.</p></article></div></section>
-</main><footer><span>JA21 2.2.1 · LOCAL_BROWSER</span><span>8 terminals max · IndexedDB virtual volume · no remote execution</span></footer>
